---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { isProduction } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout title="Our story"
  ><main id="main-content" class="wrap">
    <section class="page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">The story behind the stories</span><h1>
        Every place has a story.<br /><em>This one is ours.</em>
      </h1><p>
        All Things Sabine is a journey through the history, culture, and beauty
        of Sabine Parish, Louisiana, and the places connected to it.
      </p>
    </section><article class="about-prose">
      <img
        src="/images/stories/cropped-fullmoontrainnew.webp"
        alt="The depot and railroad tracks in Many, Louisiana, under a moonlit sky"
        width="1200"
        height="280"
      /><p>
        From forgotten communities and country stores to familiar roads and
        remarkable people, these stories preserve a little of what makes this
        corner of Louisiana home.
      </p><h2>A past worth keeping.</h2><p>
        The original story collection brings together writing and photographs by
        Shannon Hall. The Time Capsule preserves posts, photographs, and
        memories from the All Things Sabine Facebook page, with their original
        posting dates.
      </p><h2>A community still making history.</h2><p>
        Today, All Things Sabine also connects you with local restaurant menus,
        businesses, community organizations, and festivals. Each project adds
        another way to discover the people and places around us.
      </p><h2>A new chapter.</h2><p>
        {
          isProduction
            ? "Welcome to a new chapter of All Things Sabine."
            : "You’re visiting a working design preview of the next All Things Sabine."
        }
        Explore the collection, open a memory, and see how our local projects can
        come together under one roof.
      </p><a class="text-link" href="/stories/">Find your first story →</a>
    </article>
  </main></Layout
>
